Z||000035||Ayrow||12-05-2001||03:31 AM||||Interesting info???....<P>Let's see, most people probably know this, but you can pull the codes by jumping the connector under the cigar lighter with a paperclip.<P>Also,<BR>I had a red '84 2m4.  It was definately red, I remember it.<BR>In fact I have a picture of it below...<P>What do you mean they didn't make them in '84???<P>Ayrow<BR> <A HREF="http://www.ayrow.com/fiero.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.ayrow.com/fiero.html</A> ||||reg||10
Z||000036||artherd||12-05-2001||04:09 AM||||The headlights in Fieros switch between high and low beams not with a relay like in every other car, but with a solid state transistor device!  You cannot have one on at the same time as the other.<P>The 87-88 headlamps can be 'ajusted' to come up to any height you want.  you can make the lights open 'halfway'<P>Best!<BR>Ben<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000037||fierospeeder||12-05-2001||04:19 AM||||fieros didn't come with a cup holder.<P>the 84s can go as fast as the speed of light, and the friction caused so much heat that the cars burned to a crisp.<P>having sex in a manual fiero is dangerous.  She might find the shifter more satisfying then the owner.<P>intelligent people own fieros<P>fiero was originally an economy car<P>it was going to be called the sunbird<P>some fieros are friends with herbie the love bug.<P>Cops pull over fieros more then any other cars.  (unless its just me)<P>a fiero was used as a pace car, a ricer will never get that pleasure.  <P>------------------<BR>Fiero Technician<P>74 Vw Beetle<BR>83 Honda Nighthawk 550<BR>84 Pontiac Fiero<BR>87 Ford Thunderbird Turbo<P>Selling a car is like giving your own kid for adoption.||||reg||1
Z||000038||LZeitgeist||12-05-2001||06:42 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>it was going to be called the sunbird<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>BZZZZT!! Wrong...<P>It was going to be called the 'Pegasus', and that's why the nose badge appears as it does. They took the time to change the name, but not the logo designed to go with the name they had originally chosen.||||reg||1
Z||000039||Indy-2M4||12-05-2001||07:11 AM||||Only the '84's had actual "GLASS" sail panels.<P>------------------<BR>Kathy<BR>http:\\sofa.iwarp.com<BR>    <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/IndyCrueSig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000040||AusFiero||12-05-2001||08:01 AM||||When a Fiero is converted to right hand drive the heaters stop working in 99% of conversions.<BR>Volvo steering racks are almost a bolt on fit in Fieros.<BR>86 model Fiero GTs burn too if left in a burning garage  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_dizzy.gif"><P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero3.gif">       <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000041||thomas_l||12-05-2001||09:19 AM||||That weird black plastic thingy clipped under the hood above the a/c gear is a wind deflector that snaps into the slots vacated when you remove the sunroof. And the rubber strip under the hood holds the glass firmly in place when you stow the roof in there.<P>Boy did I feel stupid after riding around for a few days laying the glass in the rear trunk and getting wind blasted  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">||||reg||11
Z||000042||LZeitgeist||12-05-2001||09:48 AM||||The locking lugnut/key set originally came in a light blue sealed plastic bag. <P>The decal sets for the 1984 Indy Pace Car Replicas came uninstalled from the factory, rolled up in the trunk of the car, and was up to the dealer to install. Some installed the decals before the cars were put on the lot, some left the decals in the trunk to be installed if the owner requested, some kept the decals and put them into parts stock to sell separately from the car and never told the owner that the decal set was included with the price of the car.<P>Goodyear Eagle GT+4's were the original stock tires put on the 1988 GT's and Formulas from the factory.<P>Original factory headlights (on the '88's, at least) have the name 'Guide' in the center of the lens.<P> ||||reg||1
Z||000043||Pyric||12-05-2001||09:49 AM||||Most of you already know this... but the motors for the Fieros' headlights were originally taken from a firebird and put on opposite sides of the car.   I.e. the right fiero headlight motor is the same as the left firebird motor.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000044||LZeitgeist||12-05-2001||10:19 AM||||Also, Fieros owned Formula88 for ten years before Formula88 owned a Fiero.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000045||JohnF||12-05-2001||10:28 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LZeitgeist:<BR><B>The locking lugnut/key set originally came in a light blue sealed plastic bag. <P> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The bag also contained a stiff cardboard insert to prevent the lug key from tearing up the bag (I still have all 3 pieces).<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1578096&a=12001112&p=56509969&Sequence=0"> ||||reg||10
Z||000046||MinnGreenGT||12-05-2001||10:53 AM||||Some "factory prototypes" of the Fiero were labeled as a Mitsubishi Sprint (think there are photos in Gary Witzenberg's "Fiero" book).<P>The trunk was originally designed in the front of the car, with the spare tire being placed in the rear... the criteria was to be able to hold a golf bag w/clubs.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>There does exist a set of "Fiero Luggage" (some forum member even has one) that was designed to fit/fill the trunk perfectly!<P>'84 Fieros didn't have clothing hanger clips behind the seats- later models did!<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000047||malacite||12-05-2001||11:55 AM||||my fiero came equipped with a $.34 cent rebate, and a Blimpe hat. i still have the hat.<P>fieros are dump-truck speed bumps.<BR>luckly i moved mine just in time.||||reg||6
Z||000048||LZeitgeist||12-05-2001||12:28 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>There does exist a set of "Fiero Luggage" (some forum member even has one) that was designed to fit/fill the trunk perfectly!<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That's me!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000049||Tigger||12-05-2001||12:47 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MinnGreenGT:<BR><B>'84 Fieros didn't have clothing hanger clips behind the seats- later models did!<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Odd, I'm almost certain my '84 SE had them because I didn't want to put them back in.  Well, I could be wrong, it might have been something a previous owner added, like the third brake light.<P>I think the 84's didn't have pockets on the back of the seats.<P>84's had the center stripes down the middle of the seats.<P>At least one 85 SE was blue from the factory.  In another thread, there was talk of one of these Fieros had been found and is being restored.<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 12-05-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000050||MinnGreenGT||12-05-2001||12:54 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Tigger:<BR>[B]  At least one 85 SE was blue from the factory.  In another thread, there was talk of one of these Fieros had been found and is being restored.<BR>[B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BlueCoupe01.jpg"> <BR>Original Blue 85 Coupe!<P>Apparantly in '85 there were 5-7(?) cars done with custom factory paint... they were voted on for the next model year's colors.  I read (in the other thread I think...) that they were given/sold to factory workers! cool.||||reg||1
Z||000051||84Bill||12-05-2001||12:58 PM||||In 1984 so many fieros were produced that they ran out of the "turbo" wheels and had to switch to "Sharks tooth?" and steel wheels with trim rings. It is also alleged that this is the supposed reason the Indy Fieros possibly did not make it to the questionable 2000 possible units.... allegedly.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><BR>Oh and a credit card or like can be used to open a stuck fuel door.||||reg||1
