Z||000088||Dumba$$||12-06-2001||10:32 AM||||i used to have a print out sheet, (i think the wife tossed it out when we moved -that  p!sses me off!!!)<BR>that had every year and how many of each color were produiced<BR>all i can remember from it is there were 69,xxx red 84's made  2-bright red 87's (one was given away as a coke-a-cola promo.<BR>i think that there was 35,xxx white 84,s <BR>and it did list that there was 5-7 cars from each year that were set aside for experimantal colors, so that would probibly explane the blue 85, <BR>im not sure on ##'s butt i remember that there were only half as many gold 87's as there were 86's<BR>and i think silver was the rarest color for 84<BR>damn i wish that i had that sheet, it was posted from the fiero-list and i printed it out<P>------------------<BR>Rich<BR>Sioux Falls SD<BR>Red 84 SE<BR>Gold 86 SE <BR>98 acura cl 3.0<P>4.9 caddy engine for sale 30,000 miles complete with bubba joes mounts!!  $750||||reg||1
Z||000089||MinnGreenGT||12-06-2001||11:25 AM||||The "last two" Fieros produced were Red 88 GT's with T-Tops.  They were given to two of the factory workers through a drawing.  The inside of every body panel on the last 2 cars were signed by the employees at the plant.  Sadly, the last 2 Fieros were not "numerically" ordered to be the last 2 VIN numbers... so they have since disappeared!  I'm not aware of anyone who has been able to locate either of these car or their VIN numbers.<P>-------------------------------------<BR>The last Fiero rolled off the assembly line on August 16th 1988.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>-------------------------------------<BR>During the 1987 Fiero Festival, participants were given the opportunity to drive their Fieros through the assembly plant! This has never been done by any other car club at any other automotive plant!||||reg||1
Z||000090||Pyric||12-06-2001||11:56 AM||||A day that will live in infamy.||||reg||1
