Z||000132||paulmckibben||12-08-2001||12:39 AM||||The Fiero may not have the most web sites on the Net.  Below are results from searches using the Google search engine about two months ago.  The searches were made using the names exactly as shown.  Searches on similar names would yield different results.  (I.e. "VW Beetle" would yield different results than "Volkswagen Beetle".)  And a "hit" does not mean a website is devoted to that particular vehicle, just that the name appears on a site somewhere.  The data are not conclusive, but indicative.<P>VEHICLE	"Hits" on Google Search Engine<P>Porsche	    1,050,000<BR>Mustang	      792,000<BR>Miata	        563,000<BR>Corvette	     496,000<BR>Camaro	       331,000<BR>Firebird	     239,000<BR>Honda Accord	 123,000<BR>RX7	          113,000<BR>Fiero	         78,800<BR>VW Beetle      39,400 ("Volkswagen" got over 1 million hits)<BR>Corvair	       22,400<BR>Pontiac GTO	   21,200<BR>Dodge Neon	    21,200<BR>Ford Probe	    19,300<BR>XKE	           13,500<P>Paul McKibben<BR>Norcross, GA||||reg||1
