Z||000137||kslish||12-09-2001||03:19 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MinnGreenGT:<BR><B>The "last two" Fieros produced were Red 88 GT's with T-Tops.  They were given to two of the factory workers through a drawing.  The inside of every body panel on the last 2 cars were signed by the employees at the plant.  Sadly, the last 2 Fieros were not "numerically" ordered to be the last 2 VIN numbers... so they have since disappeared!  I'm not aware of anyone who has been able to locate either of these car or their VIN numbers.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well, at least one of them hasn't disappeared...<P>Here is an article about the last Fiero that rolled off the assembly line and the Fiero plant truck driver that it was given to:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.michiganfieroclub.org/lastfiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.michiganfieroclub.org/lastfiero.htm</A> <P>Incidentaly, this Fiero has appeared for sale in Hemmings Motor News a few times over the past few years but never sold as far as I know (I believe he was asking somewhere around $25,000 for it).<P>Ken S.||||reg||1
Z||000138||Reality||12-09-2001||07:14 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MinnGreenGT:<BR><B>The "last two" Fieros produced were Red 88 GT's with T-Tops.  They were given to two of the factory workers through a drawing.  The inside of every body panel on the last 2 cars were signed by the employees at the plant.  Sadly, the last 2 Fieros were not "numerically" ordered to be the last 2 VIN numbers... so they have since disappeared!  I'm not aware of anyone who has been able to locate either of these car or their VIN numbers.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I thought the VIN for the last two cars were:<BR>1G2PG1193JP226401<BR>and<BR>1G2PG1193JP226402<p>[This message has been edited by Reality (edited 12-09-2001).]||||reg||1
